      "module": "ibuffer",
      "definition": "There are eight independent warp banks, each with a queue of at most two fetched pairs and one active pair. rst_n is asynchronous active-low: assertion immediately clears every queued pair, queue occupancy, active payload and active lane eligibility. All output payload fields are zero after reset. A high ibuffer_flush_wid_valid_i at a rising edge clears exactly the bank selected by the three-bit ibuffer_flush_wid_i, including both pending and active data. Flush dominates enqueue, queue-to-active loading and retirement on that bank. Other banks continue their own normal operations. Release reset away from rising edges; a flush is synchronous and cannot change state before its edge.",
